# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
# S-D5: PyInstaller auto-writes this beside the entry point it's given
# (scripts/freeze.py's own invocation) -- a regenerated build artifact,
# same reasoning as build/dist above, and it embeds an absolute machine
# path (P-2) so it must never be committed.
/vantage.spec

# Test / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Conan local
conaninfo.txt
conanbuildinfo.*
conan.lock

# Editors / OS
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Local run output (recordings, snapshots, exports are never committed here —
# they belong to the component under test, e.g. modules/df/tests/)
*.mcap
*.png
*.mp4

# Ad hoc test logs / human-review screenshots (AI-session working notes,
# never source) -- colocated here instead of a folder outside the repo so
# they stay easy to find and are still guaranteed never committed.
#
# ANCHORED (AR-6). Unanchored `logs/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, so it also swallowed docs/py/logs/ -- which docs/py/README.md declares
# to be "committed output, the proof ... append-only". The observable result:
# the 2026-07-28/07-29 evidence logs are tracked and every run since was
# silently not, with `git status` clean the whole time. The leading slash pins
# this to modules/sim/logs/, which is the directory the comment above is about.
/logs/

# Exception: the framework's own self-contained fixture (S-A4,
# sim_implementation_plan.md §3.3) -- generated by make_tiny_mcap.py, never
# hand-crafted, but committed so the suite needs no real component build.
!tests/fixtures/tiny.mcap

# Machine-local pointer to a reference tool installation (DC-2: no absolute
# paths in the repo). See docs/py/_common.py:reference_tool_root().
docs/py/reference_tool_path.txt
scripts/gui_config.json
